      en: "Delta Beverages in Bulawayo operates multiple strategic production units, including lager breweries, traditional sorghum beer plants, and sparkling beverage bottling lines. As the second-largest hub for Delta Corporation, this location serves as the primary supply point for the western and southern regions of Zimbabwe. A notable component is the Chibuku traditional beer brewery, which produces the popular sorghum-based drink through close partnerships with local smallholder farmers. The facilities, situated in the Belmont and Steeldale industrial areas, employ advanced processing technology to maintain rigorous quality standards. Delta Beverages remains one of the most resilient large-scale industrial employers in Bulawayo, playing a pivotal role in the city's economic ecosystem. The site's logistics division coordinates an extensive distribution network that ensures product availability even in remote rural districts. Recent investments in high-efficiency glass bottling lines have significantly boosted throughput and reduced operational costs. The company also spearheads regional community initiatives and promotes a circular economy through extensive bottle-return and recycling programs.",
